21,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems the roads north of the river are quite unreliable in winter, though the halls there managed to stay open.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The outer wards have lost their bus links, making it very difficult for some residents to reach us.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Rin,,"We tried digitizing photos years ago and it was a mess, but some evening groups are still going strong!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Our vehicle costs are overrunning, and the grants only cover session fees for a year before the main budget takes over.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Minako,,"We have skilled volunteers for repairs, but we lack staff trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, if the buses are gone, those people must feel very isolated from our services.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Exactly, Shizue. The distance is now a significant barrier for the outer wards.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, does that mean we can't afford things that last a long time?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It means we must be wary of ""temporary"" grants that create permanent costs we cannot sustain.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, it also means we should check if we have the actual skills to run a new program.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, it is a shame we have the volunteers but not the supervisors to guide them.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I also noticed that people are using the catalogue late at night, long after we have locked the doors.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Rin,,I found that outreach stops used to be way more popular than the main building during the week!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, that suggests a demand for services that doesn't fit our current physical footprint.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I also found that our tool certification expert has retired, which is a worrying gap.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Shizue,,We must find a way to reach people that doesn't fall apart when the weather turns or the buses stop.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. The current system is too rigid for the people who need us most.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Rin,,Let's not repeat the mistakes of the photo project! We need something that actually works.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates we avoid high-maintenance vehicles and short-term funding traps.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Minako,,And we must avoid anything requiring specialized certifications we no longer possess.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
46,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
48,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
49,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The candidates are A: Mobile Branch, B: Maker Workshop, C: Language Circles, and D: Digital Archive. I worry A is too weather-dependent.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"A addresses the bus issue, but D addresses the late-night catalogue use. I lean toward A for the outer wards.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Rin,,I don't like D because the old digitisation project failed. C sounds like those evening groups that are still working!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,A has high running costs and D has delivery risks. C's funding model is the most concerning if it relies on grants.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Minako,,B requires tool certification we lack. C requires supervisors we don't have. D is the most stable for staff.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, if the roads close, the Mobile Branch cannot reach the people. That is a fragile plan.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"That is true, Shizue. But the need in the outer wards is so great.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, but wouldn't a Digital Archive be boring? The Language Circles sound like a real adventure!","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, adventure is lovely, but sustainability is better. C's session fees will eventually drain our operating budget.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, A's vehicle costs are already overrunning in our current ledgers. It is a financial liability.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I feel C is a gentle way to bring people together, provided we can find the facilitators.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If A is too expensive and fragile, perhaps C is the best compromise for community reach.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for C! It's like the groups that survived for six years.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"D is the most logically sound, as it avoids vehicle costs and staffing gaps.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Minako,,I agree with Benjamin. D is the only one that doesn't create a new staffing or financial crisis.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will support C. It brings the community together without needing a bus.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will also vote for C. It serves the people who cannot reach the branch.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Rin,,C is the best!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I remain with D, but I see the consensus shifting.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Minako,,I stand by D. It is the only responsible choice.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
